  "title": "U.S.-China Geopolitical Tensions and Summit Dynamics",
  "summary": "The U.S.-China Trump-Xi summit in Washington, D.C., aimed to address key global issues, but discussions around potential arms sales and strategic moves have sparked geopolitical tensions. The summit also highlighted the ongoing U.S.-Iran conflict and the need for tangible outcomes to foster a truce. The U.S., China, and Russia will meet in New York for the Trump-Xi summit, while global leaders will hold back-to-back diplomatic summits in Asia to address trade, tech and regional security.",
