  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "World leaders head to Asia for back-to-back diplomatic summits",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/15/asia-diplomatic-summits-trump-xi-putin-apec-asean",
      "description": "<p>Tussle for influence as trade, tech and regional security to take centre stage in China, Philippines and Cambodia meetings</p><p>World leaders will fly in to Asia for back-to-back high-level summits this week against the backdrop of the tussle for influence between the superpowers China and the US.</p><p>Beijing will have the home advantage when it welcomes Donald Trump to its southern technology hub of Shenzhen for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (Apec) leaders’ meeting. It starts two weeks after the US leader <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-midterm-elections-2026\">lost midterm elections</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/15/asia-diplomatic-summits-trump-xi-putin-apec-asean\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-15T04:00:02"
    },
    {
      "title": "Anthony Albanese welcomes Trump-Xi-Putin summit – even as European leaders express reservations",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/anthony-albanese-welcomes-trump-xi-putin-summit-even-as-european-leaders-express-reservations",
      "description": "<p>‘We think dialogue is a good thing,’ Australian PM says after German chancellor urges the US to work with Europe for peace in Ukraine</p><p>Australia has endorsed this week’s historic summit between Donald Trump, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin in China, even as European leaders warn that the US president must not make major concessions over the war in Ukraine.</p><p>The three-way summit is planned to take place in Shenzhen, where the leaders will gather for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (Apec) meeting. The Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelenskyy, has warned the talks must not lead to a redistribution of influence among world powers or the abandonment of his country, more than four years into the war sparked by Putin’s full-scale invasion.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/15/anthony-albanese-welcomes-trump-xi-putin-summit-even-as-european-leaders-express-reservations\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-15T06:22:32"
    }
  ]
